      "author": "Swami Vivekananda",
      "work": "Jnana Yoga",
      "edition": "16th Edition",
      "publisher": "Advaita Ashrama",
      "section": "Volume 1",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ramakrishnamath.in/cwsv"
    },
    "text": "You have to grow from the inside out. None can teach you, none can make you spiritual. There is no other teacher but your own soul.",
    "locationLabel": "Volume 1, Jnana Yoga, Chapter I",
    "language": "en",
    "topics": [
      "self_belief",
      "decision",
      "confusion",
      "purpose"
    ],
    "verified": true
  },
  {
    "id": "VIV_011",
    "source": {
      "title": "Complete Works of Swami Vivekananda",
      "author": "Swami Vivekananda",
      "work": "Lectures from Colombo to Almora",
      "edition": "15th Edition",
      "publisher": "Advaita Ashrama",
      "section": "Volume 3",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ramakrishnamath.in/cwsv"
    },
    "text": "All power is within you; you can do anything and everything. Believe in that, do not believe that you are weak; do not believe that you are half-crazy giants, as most of us do nowadays. You can do any thing and everything, without even the guidance of any one.",
    "locationLabel": "Volume 3, Work Before Us",
    "language": "en",
    "topics": [
      "self_belief",
      "motivation",
      "strength"
    ],
    "verified": true
  },
